# VPN_SWITCH_KEEPALIVE_wireguard - PersistentKeepalive for patched configs
#
# Injected into patched WireGuard configs as "PersistentKeepalive = <value>"
# (seconds) when the source config does not set PersistentKeepalive itself.
#
# Default: 25 (the wg(8)-recommended value for NAT / stateful-firewall traversal)
#
# Rationale: Provider configs (e.g. ProtonVPN) ship without PersistentKeepalive.
# Behind NAT or on flapping links (WLAN) the tunnel then stays silent after a
# link drop; stateful gateways expire the UDP mapping and the tunnel appears
# dead until it is rebuilt by hand.
#
# Behavior:
#   - A PersistentKeepalive line in the source config always wins (never overridden)
#   - Set to 0 to disable injection entirely
#   - Non-numeric values fall back to the default
#   - Injected at the end of the config, i.e. into the last [Peer] section;
#     multi-peer configs should set the value per peer in the config itself
#   - Applies to both the session patch (connect) and 'wireguard patch' output
